⚠️ **IMPORTANT: RT4/RT5 skip the re-anchor the copied pattern guards with — the residual flake window the pattern exists for**

`typeSecret` (copied from the gh-1244/#1245 precedent) re-anchors once when the anchored frame predates the value row's closing border — that race was real enough to earn a review-thread fix upstream:

```dart
if (maskedValueRow(screen) == null) {
  screen = await harness.waitForScreen('•' * secret.length, ...);
}
```

Both new sites filter/read through the **same `│`-closed guard** but never re-anchor:

- **RT4** (this line): `maskedRows` keeps only rows with `trimRight().endsWith('│')`. If the first frame containing `'•' * 19` predates one of the value rows' closing border by a repaint (the exact case the pattern tolerates), that row silently drops out of the list and the exact pin `[19, 6, 17]` fails — a new flake in the very suite this PR de-flakes, and a harder-to-diagnose one (the failure message shows a partial list, not a null row).
- **RT5** (`maskedValueRow(screen)` below): a null row throws `StateError` — loud, but still a hard failure on the same one-frame race instead of the one-shot re-anchor.

The window is narrow (a single 50 ms poll boundary on a loaded runner), but it is the identical class gh-1244's review thread fixed, and these tests run on exactly those loaded CI shards. Cheapest fix: one re-anchor before the row-dependent reads, mirroring `typeSecret`:

```dart
var screen = await harness.waitForScreen('•' * 19, timeout: ...);
if (maskedValueRow(screen) == null) {
  screen = await harness.waitForScreen('•' * 19, timeout: ...);
}
```

